---
import '../styles/kit.css';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import LinkCard from '../components/LinkCard.astro';
import { href, GITHUB_URL } from '../lib/site';

---

<Page path="/what-it-checks">
	<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
	    <div class="bd first"><div class="wrap"><h1 class="t60">What a11ign checks, and how it fits your tech stack</h1></div></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="miss"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="miss" class="t36">What a screen reader catches that code checks miss</h2></div>
	<ul class="rows"><li><h3>A skip link that does nothing</h3><p>It looks right in the code, but pressing it goes nowhere. <span class="hl">Code checks pass while a screen reader user is stuck.</span></p></li><li><h3>A page change nobody hears</h3><p>The page updates but the title doesn’t, so nobody is told where they are now.</p></li><li><h3>A filter or form that says nothing</h3><p>Results change or an error appears, and nothing is read out.</p></li><li><h3>Tab order that fights reading order</h3><p>The order you tab through the page and the order it’s read out disagree, and only a real walkthrough shows it.</p></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="how"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="how" class="t36">How a finding is decided</h2></div>
	<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px"><strong>Asserted:</strong> the evidence settles it, so the report says the rule isn’t met. <strong>Referred:</strong> the evidence points to a problem but a person should decide, so the report quotes the words and points you to them.</p><p class="muted">What we’ve measured: across 1,405 records of pages that meet the standard, the exact rules raised no false alarms. That’s our own test set. Most findings are marked referred, and that’s expected.</p><p><a class="lnk2 solo" href={href('/docs/how-we-know-it-works')}>See the work behind these numbers</a></p>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd alt"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="stack"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="stack" class="t36">Fits inside your tech stack</h2></div>
	<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">a11ign adds to the tools you already use. It doesn’t replace them.</p><ul class="grid"><li><Card title={"GitHub Actions"}>One step in your workflow, on a Windows runner GitHub provides. The report appears as a pull request comment, and the results are saved with the run.</Card></li><li><Card title="axe-core">Run it next to axe-core, or feed in the axe-core results you already have, so you still have one engine and one version.</Card></li><li><Card title={"Command line"}>Run it with npx from your own Windows machine with NVDA, when you want it outside CI.</Card></li><li><Card title={"Playwright tests"}>Coming soon: the quick check predicts what NVDA would say inside the Playwright tests you already run.</Card></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="two"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="two" class="t36">Two ways to check</h2></div>
	<table class="cmp"><thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="sr" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px">Row</span></th><th scope="col">Real NVDA run</th><th scope="col">Quick check <span class="pill pred">Coming soon</span></th></tr></thead><tbody>
	<tr><th scope="row">What it does</th><td data-l="Real NVDA run">Drives real NVDA and records what it said</td><td data-l="Quick check">Predicts what NVDA would say, in the browser</td></tr>
	<tr><th scope="row">Its output is</th><td data-l="Real NVDA run">Proof: the words NVDA said</td><td data-l="Quick check">A prediction, always labelled</td></tr>
	<tr><th scope="row">Runs on</th><td data-l="Real NVDA run">A Windows machine, or one GitHub provides</td><td data-l="Quick check">Any operating system, planned for your Playwright tests</td></tr>
	<tr><th scope="row">Best used</th><td data-l="Real NVDA run">Before a release and on key flows</td><td data-l="Quick check">On every commit</td></tr>
	<tr><th scope="row">Measured</th><td data-l="Real NVDA run">A run takes 105 to 460 seconds of machine time per page</td><td data-l="Quick check">99.71% agreement on the 10 most common kinds of announcement (3,497 of 3,507), on pages it was not tuned to. Speed not measured yet</td></tr>
	</tbody></table>
	<a class="lnk solo" href={href('/docs')} style="color:var(--link);font-weight:600">Read how the quick check was measured</a>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="not"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="not" class="t36">What to expect</h2></div>
	<ul class="list"><li>Proof, not a score: every finding quotes what the screen reader said.</li><li>Evidence you can act on, alongside your own judgement and legal advice.</li><li>Focused on the pages you choose, like checkout, sign-up and search.</li><li>Built to sit beside your other checks. Run it with axe-core, which covers colour contrast.</li><li>One screen reader, done properly: NVDA today. Braille, magnification and voice control aren’t covered yet.</li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="deeper"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="deeper" class="t36">Go deeper</h2></div>
	<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">Want to see the work behind it, or how to set it up? Start here.</p><ul class="grid g3"><li><LinkCard title={"How we know it works"} description={"How we trained and tested a11ign, with the numbers."} href={href('/docs/how-we-know-it-works')} cue="Read" /></li><li><LinkCard title={"GitHub Action guide"} description={"The workflow file, the settings you will use, and what you get back."} href={href('/docs/github-action')} cue="Read" /></li><li><LinkCard title={"Why we built it"} description={"What we believe, how it is built, and what is next."} href={href('/about')} cue="Read" /></li></ul>
	    </section></div>
	    <div class="bd"><section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="fit"><div class="sh"><span class="num ico" aria-hidden="true"></span><h2 id="fit" class="t36">Where it fits</h2></div>
	<p class="lead" style="font-size:20px">Run the real check on key flows like checkout, sign-up and search, before a release, or as proof for an audit. Keep your fast code checks on every commit.</p><div class="ctaRow"><Button size="lg" href={href('/get-started')}>Add to your workflow</Button><Button size="lg" variant="secondary" icon="github" href={GITHUB_URL}>Star on GitHub</Button></div>
	    </section></div>
	  </main>
</Page>

